arning tool to predict appropriate height and weight from chest radiographs in bedridden patients#🔵 Sonuç / Conclusions (Mavi)":[38,40],"#Development of deep-learning tool to predict appropriate height and weight from chest radiographs in bedridden patients#🔵 Sonuç / Conclusions (Mavi)#{1}":[39,40],"#Development of deep-learning tool to predict appropriate height and weight from chest radiographs in bedridden patients#🟠 Limitasyonlar (Turuncu)":[41,42]},"outlinks":[{"title":"Görüntüle","target":"zotero://select/library/items/55QME7ZY","line":22},{"title":"Sayfa 1","target":"zotero://open-pdf/library/items/NKZAY27V?page=1&annotation=H2DKV6TX","line":33},{"title":"Sayfa 1","target":"zotero://open-pdf/library/items/NKZAY27V?page=1&annotation=SCLYD6PR","line":33},{"title":"Sayfa 2","target":"zotero://open-pdf/library/items/NKZAY27V?page=2&annotation=W6AA79V7","line":36},{"title":"Sayfa 2","target":"zotero://open-pdf/library/items/NKZAY27V?page=2&annotation=2T7NKGM6","line":39}],"metadata":{"Title":"Development of deep-learning tool to predict appropriate height and weight from chest radiographs in bedridden patients","Authors":"Yasuhiko Nakao, Ryo Sasaki, Fumihiro Mawatari, Kotaro Harakawa, Minoru Okita, Norisato Mitsutake, Kazuhiko Nakao","Year":2023,"DOI":"10.1016/j.nutos.2023.08.005","Nitelik":null,"Alan":null,"Konu":null,"AI_Methodology":null,"Layer_Focus":null,"Model_Asamasi":null,"Proposed_Tool":null,"Methods":"This study aimed to illustrate the potential of a convolutional neural network model to assess the height and weight based on chest radiographs.A convolutional neural network was used to predict the height and weight of the patients (Juzen NST). A ResNet152 classifier was trained using Fastai (V1.0) running on PyTorch to predict the height and weight. Training was performed for four epochs using validation without augmentation.","Findings":"Our chest radiographic prediction model has a high correlation with actual height and weight and can be combined with information regarding clinical nutrition factors for rapid assessment of risk for malnutrition","Conclusions":"area. Importantly, our model is an illustration of the potential of automated imaging artificial intelligence for proper nutrition prediction models in older adults.","Limitations":"","User_Notes":""},"task_lines":[],"tasks":{},"codeblock_ranges":[],"last_embed":{"hash":"b6ab6w","at":1774939666250}},"smart_blocks:nakaoDevelopmentDeeplearningTool2023a.md#---frontmatter---": {"path":null,"embeddings":{"TaylorAI/bge-micro-v2":{"vec":[-0.05201792,0.03212341,-0.00347568,0.01303062,0.02372738,0.01743902,-0.01828407,0.01739694,-0.00823996,-0.00846901,0.00495758,-0.1043417,-0.01134851,0.07811502,0.05121414,-0.00629281,0.02876017,0.03272702,-0.03589096,0.03356538,0.05235062,0.01363912,0.01966683,-0.05403608,0.07639353,-0.05409781,0.00037573,-0.06371323,-0.05903833,-0.2324176,0.0706019,-0.03060707,0.08472453,-0.01151972,-0.03745315,0.00434065,0.00905678,0.05500813,-0.016968,0.04428646,-0.00564896,0.03650236,0.01290724,-0.00247003,0.04222036,-0.02408366,-0.02233417,-0.05216046,-0.03394878,0.05825167,-0.03353639,-0.04880955,0.02196405,0.06954376,0.03246728,-0.0103923,0.05437202,0.01839055,0.07139449,0.06344145,-0.00023106,0.07375053,-0.20274208,0.04913746,0.04657001,0.04722992,-0.04617545,0.00675448,0.03461483,0.01760619,0.02235241,0.03728025,0.06182232,0.04336832,0.00645413,0.0026169,0.02003818,-0.02307159,0.00251058,-0.03878799,0.01653244,0.06649353,-0.04741496,-0.03152925,-0.03803536,-0.03455989,-0.02728166,-0.06384538,-0.00655039,-0.02529329,-0.05316332,-0.02884908,-0.05747345,0.04524903,-0.03933296,0.00136487,0.03107554,0.01770823,-0.10083992,0.09328918,-0.01817168,0.01980746,0.0328607,-0.01116186,0.03614257,-0.04997798,-0.04321202,-0.05205641,0.00699894,0.03797479,-0.0358927,-0.00613845,-0.03441131,0.01158466,-0.01992039,0.04095953,0.05849392,0.0714209,-0.00512878,-0.00482873,-0.05439648,-0.02594906,0.04390416,-0.01165524,0.01024944,-0.01489778,-0.02726526,0.0963